"default")),Name("pp"),Type(concTypeOption(),"unknown type",EmptyTargetLanguageType()))),CompositeTL(ITL(".getHead()"))),BuildEmptyList(Name("PathTerm")))))),TargetLanguageToCode(TL(";\n        pp = pp.getTail();\n      }\n      return (PathTerm) ref;\n    }\n\n    public int compare(Path p) {\n      Position p1 = Position.makeFromPath(this);\n      Position p2 = Position.makeFromPath(p);\n      return p1.compare(p2);\n    }\n    \n\n\n  /**\n   * Returns the number of arguments of the variadic operator\n   *\n   * @return the number of arguments of the variadic operator\n   */\n  @Override\n  public int length() {\n    int res = 0;\n    gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term tl = this;\n    while(tl instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      res += 1;\n      tl = tl.getTailPathTerm();\n      if(tl instanceof PathTerm == false) {\n        res += 1;\n      }\n    }\n    return res;\n/*\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term tl = this.getTailPathTerm();\n      if (tl instanceof PathTerm) {\n        return 1+((PathTerm)tl).length();\n      } else {\n        return 2;\n      }\n    } else {\n      return 0;\n    }\n    */\n  }\n\n  public static gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term fromArray(int[] array) {\n    gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm.make();\n    for(int i = array.length; i>0;) {\n      res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(array[--i],res);\n    }\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Inverses the term if it is a list\n   *\n   * @return the inverted term if it is a list, otherwise the term itself\n   */\n  @Override\n  public gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term reverse() {\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term cur = this;\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term rev = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm.make();\n      while(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n        rev = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(cur.getHeadPathTerm(),rev);\n        cur = cur.getTailPathTerm();\n      }\n\n      return rev;\n    } else {\n      return this;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Appends an element\n   *\n   * @param element element which has to be added\n   * @return the term with the added element\n   */\n  public gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term append(int element) {\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term tl = this.getTailPathTerm();\n      if (tl instanceof PathTerm) {\n        return gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(this.getHeadPathTerm(),((PathTerm)tl).append(element));\n      } else {\n\n        return gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(this.getHeadPathTerm(),gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(element,tl));\n\n      }\n    } else {\n      return gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(element,this);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Appends a string representation of this term to the buffer given as argument.\n   *\n   * @param buffer the buffer to which a string represention of this term is appended.\n   */\n  @Override\n  public void toStringBuilder(java.lang.StringBuilder buffer) {\n    buffer.append(\"PathTerm(\");\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term cur = this;\n      while(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n        int elem = cur.getHeadPathTerm();\n        cur = cur.getTailPathTerm();\n        buffer.append(elem);\n\n        if(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n          buffer.append(\",\");\n        }\n      }\n      if(!(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm)) {\n        buffer.append(\",\");\n        cur.toStringBuilder(buffer);\n      }\n    }\n    buffer.append(\")\");\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns an ATerm representation of this term.\n   *\n   * @return an ATerm representation of this term.\n   */\n  public aterm.ATerm toATerm() {\n    aterm.ATerm res = atermFactory.makeList();\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term tail = this.getTailPathTerm();\n      res = atermFactory.makeList((aterm.ATerm) atermFactory.makeInt(getHeadPathTerm()),(aterm.ATermList)tail.toATerm());\n    }\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Apply a conversion on the ATerm contained in the String and returns a gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term from it\n   *\n   * @param trm ATerm to convert into a Gom term\n   * @param atConv ATerm Converter used to convert the ATerm\n   * @return the Gom term\n   */\n  public static gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term fromTerm(aterm.ATerm trm, tom.library.utils.ATermConverter atConv) {\n    trm = atConv.convert(trm);\n    if(trm instanceof aterm.ATermAppl) {\n      aterm.ATermAppl appl = (aterm.ATermAppl) trm;\n      if(\"PathTerm\".equals(appl.getName())) {\n        gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm.make();\n\n        aterm.ATerm array[] = appl.getArgumentArray();\n        for(int i = array.length-1; i>=0; --i) {\n          int elem = convertATermToInt(array[i], atConv);\n          res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(elem,res);\n        }\n        return res;\n      }\n    }\n\n    if(trm instanceof aterm.ATermList) {\n      aterm.ATermList list = (aterm.ATermList) trm;\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm.make();\n      try {\n        while(!list.isEmpty()) {\n          int elem = convertATermToInt(list.getFirst(), atConv);\n          res = gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm.make(elem,res);\n          list = list.getNext();\n        }\n      } catch(IllegalArgumentException e) {\n        // returns null when the fromATerm call failed\n        return null;\n      }\n      return res.reverse();\n    }\n\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  /*\n   * Checks if the Collection contains all elements of the parameter Collection\n   *\n   * @param c the Collection of elements to check\n   * @return true if the Collection contains all elements of the parameter, otherwise false\n   */\n  public boolean containsAll(java.util.Collection c) {\n    java.util.Iterator it = c.iterator();\n    while(it.hasNext()) {\n      if(!this.contains(it.next())) {\n        return false;\n      }\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks if gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term contains a specified object\n   *\n   * @param o object whose presence is tested\n   * @return true if gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term contains the object, otherwise false\n   */\n  public boolean contains(Object o) {\n    gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term cur = this;\n    if(o==null) { return false; }\n    if(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      while(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n        if( o.equals(cur.getHeadPathTerm()) ) {\n          return true;\n        }\n        cur = cur.getTailPathTerm();\n      }\n      if(!(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm)) {\n        if( o.equals(cur) ) {\n          return true;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  //public boolean equals(Object o) { return this.deepEquals(o); }\n\n  //public int hashCode() { return hashCode(); }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks the emptiness\n   *\n   * @return true if empty, otherwise false\n   */\n  public boolean isEmpty() { return isEmptyPathTerm() ; }\n\n  public java.util.Iterator<java.lang.Integer> iterator() {\n    return new java.util.Iterator<java.lang.Integer>() {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term list = PathTerm.this;\n\n      public boolean hasNext() {\n        return list!=null && !list.isEmptyPathTerm();\n      }\n\n      public java.lang.Integer next() {\n        if(list.isEmptyPathTerm()) {\n          throw new java.util.NoSuchElementException();\n        }\n        if(list.isConsPathTerm()) {\n          java.lang.Integer head = list.getHeadPathTerm();\n          list = list.getTailPathTerm();\n          return head;\n        } else {\n          // we are in this case only if domain=codomain\n          // thus, the cast is safe\n          Object res = list;\n          list = null;\n          return (java.lang.Integer)res;\n        }\n      }\n\n      public void remove() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"Not yet implemented\");\n      }\n    };\n\n  }\n\n  public boolean add(java.lang.Integer o) {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  public boolean addAll(java.util.Collection<? extends java.lang.Integer> c) {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  public boolean remove(Object o) {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  public void clear() {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  public boolean removeAll(java.util.Collection c) {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  public boolean retainAll(java.util.Collection c) {\n    throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"This object \"+this.getClass().getName()+\" is not mutable\");\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns the size of the collection\n   *\n   * @return the size of the collection\n   */\n  public int size() { return length(); }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns an array containing the elements of the collection\n   *\n   * @return an array of elements\n   */\n  public Object[] toArray() {\n    int size = this.length();\n    Object[] array = new Object[size];\n    int i=0;\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term cur = this;\n      while(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n        java.lang.Integer elem = cur.getHeadPathTerm();\n        array[i] = elem;\n        cur = cur.getTailPathTerm();\n        i++;\n      }\n      if(!(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm)) {\n        array[i] = cur;\n      }\n    }\n    return array;\n  }\n\n  @SuppressWarnings(\"unchecked\")\n  public <T> T[] toArray(T[] array) {\n    int size = this.length();\n    if (array.length < size) {\n      array = (T[]) java.lang.reflect.Array.newInstance(array.getClass().getComponentType(), size);\n    } else if (array.length > size) {\n      array[size] = null;\n    }\n    int i=0;\n    if(this instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n      gom.testtermgraph.m.types.Term cur = this;\n      while(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.ConsPathTerm) {\n        java.lang.Integer elem = cur.getHeadPathTerm();\n        array[i] = (T)elem;\n        cur = cur.getTailPathTerm();\n        i++;\n      }\n      if(!(cur instanceof gom.testtermgraph.m.types.term.EmptyPathTerm)) {\n        array[i] = (T)cur;\n      }\n    }\n    return array;\n  }\n\n  /*\n   * to get a Collection for an immutable list\n   */\n  public java.util.Collection<java.lang.Integer> getCollection() {\n    return new CollectionPathTerm(this);\n  }\n\n  public java.util.Collection<java.lang.Integer> getCollectionPathTerm() {\n    return new CollectionPathTerm(this);\n  }\n\n  /************************************************************\n   * private static class\n   ************************************************************/\n  private static class CollectionPathTerm implements java.util.Collection<java.lang.Integer> {\n    private PathTerm list;\n\n    public PathTerm getTerm() {\n      return list;\n    }\n\n    public CollectionPathTerm(PathTerm list) {\n      this.list = list;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * generic\n     */\n  public boolean addAll(java.util.Collection<? extends java.lang.Integer> c) {\n    boolean modified = false;\n    java.util.Iterator<? extends java.lang.Integer> it = c.iterator();\n    while(it.hasNext()) {\n      modified = modified || add(it.next());\n    }\n    return modified;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks if the collection contains an element\n   *\n   * @param o element whose presence has to be checked\n   * @return true if the element is found, otherwise false\n   */\n  public boolean contains(Object o) {\n    return getTerm().contains(o);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks if the collection contains elements given as parameter\n   *\n   * @param c elements whose presence has to be checked\n   * @return true all the elements are found, otherwise false\n   */\n  public boolean containsAll(java.util.Collection<?> c) {\n    return getTerm().containsAll(c);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks if an object is equal\n   *\n   * @param o object which is compared\n   * @return true if objects are equal, false otherwise\n   */\n  @Override\n  public boolean equals(Object o) {\n    return getTerm().equals(o);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns the hashCode\n   *\n   * @return the hashCode\n   */\n  @Override\n  public int hashCode() {\n    return getTerm().hashCode();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns an iterator over the elements in the collection\n   *\n   * @return an iterator over the elements in the collection\n   */\n  public java.util.Iterator<java.lang.Integer> iterator() {\n    return getTerm().iterator();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Return the size of the collection\n   *\n   * @return the size of the collection\n   */\n  public int size() {\n    return getTerm().size();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns an array containing all of the elements in this collection.\n   *\n   * @return an array of elements\n   */\n  public Object[] toArray() {\n    return getTerm().toArray();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns an array containing all of the elements in this collection.\n   *\n   * @param array array whic